<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Description>DuckDB ADO.NET Provider for C#.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
- Updated to DuckDB v2.0.1

Upgrading from 1.x: https://duckdb.net/docs/upgrade-to-2.0.html
All changes: https://duckdb.net/docs/release-notes/2.0.html

New features:
- Int128 and UInt128 for HUGEINT and UHUGEINT, in reads, the appenders, functions and parameters (#370)
- DuckDBCommand.Prepare() prepares the statement and keeps it on the connection
- DuckDBArrowAppender appends Apache Arrow record batches and streams to a table
- TIME_NS columns (#386, #387)
- LIST, MAP and STRUCT columns are read without boxing, and the common element types work under Native AOT
- GetBytes and GetChars (#377), GetSchema("DataTypes") (#364)
- A table function over an array or a collection tells DuckDB its row count
- A timestamp table function parameter can be read as DateTimeOffset (#397)

Breaking changes:
- HUGEINT and UHUGEINT are read as Int128 and UInt128 instead of BigInteger. sum() of an integer column is a HUGEINT, so cast its result to Int128
- A BLOB is read as byte[] instead of Stream. GetStream still returns a stream
- A FLOAT, DOUBLE or DECIMAL value with a fractional part, read as an integer type, throws InvalidCastException instead of being rounded
- A DbType set on a parameter is kept when Value is assigned afterwards (#369), and decides the value. A value that doesn't fit the DbType, such as 2.5 with DbType.Int32, throws InvalidCastException
- IDuckDBAppenderRow has new AppendValue overloads for Int128, UInt128, DateOnly and TimeOnly. With C# 12 an integer constant passed to AppendValue is ambiguous, so give it the type of its column, for example (int?)1
- DuckDBDateOnly and DuckDBTimeOnly convert to DateOnly and TimeOnly only explicitly
- A typed scalar function with no nullable parameter returns NULL for a NULL argument without being called. Declare the parameter string? or mark it [AllowNull] to be called
- ExecuteNonQuery returns -1 for statements other than INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, MERGE and COPY (#374)
- CardinalityHint.IsExact = false is now an estimate, and true an exact count that DuckDB also takes as a maximum
- Parameter values, list items, map entries and struct fields are converted more strictly. See the upgrade guide

Fixes:
- A string with NUL characters is stored in full. It was cut at the first NUL
- A BigInteger appended to a column other than HUGEINT or UHUGEINT throws. Its 16 bytes overwrote the values next to it
- A date written to a TIME, TIMETZ or timestamp column, a time written to a DATE, TIMETZ or timestamp column, and a DateTime written to a TIMETZ column throw instead of storing wrong values. A DateTime appended to a TIME column stores its time of day
- A STRUCT read into a C# struct gets the values of its fields
- A byte[] returned by a scalar or table function is written to a BLOB column (#395)

Thanks to Alaric Dailey (@alaricd) for his pull requests that brought DuckDB.NET's ADO.NET behaviour in line with the documented contracts, and to Michał Rusinek (@Mr444-dev) for TIME_NS support.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <SignAssembly>True</SignAssembly>
    <AssemblyOriginatorKeyFile>..\keyPair.snk</AssemblyOriginatorKeyFile>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(BuildType)' == 'ManagedOnly' ">
    <Description>$(Description) $(NoNativeText)</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);CI</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">
    <PackageReference Include="GitVersion.MsBuild" Version="6.4.0" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="DuckDB.NET.Test, " />
    <!-- The signed benchmark assembly needs internal mappings to reproduce the pre-AppendRow baseline. -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Apache.Arrow" Version="23.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DuckDB.NET.Bindings\Bindings.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Data and Bindings ship together, and Data needs the Bindings of its own major version: Data 1.5.x, whose
       dependency had no upper bound, failed with TypeLoadException under Bindings 2.0. NuGet takes a project
       reference's version as a minimum, so the range is set on the item pack builds the dependency from. -->
  <Target Name="LimitBindingsToThisMajorVersion" AfterTargets="_GetProjectReferenceVersions">
    <PropertyGroup>
      <_NextMajorVersion>$([MSBuild]::Add($(PackageVersion.Split('.')[0]), 1)).0.0</_NextMajorVersion>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
      <_ProjectReferencesWithVersions Condition="'%(Filename)' == 'Bindings'">
        <ProjectVersion>[%(ProjectVersion), $(_NextMajorVersion))</ProjectVersion>
      </_ProjectReferencesWithVersions>
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
